# viki's derived cache is UNENCRYPTED, key-free, and a complete plaintext
# copy of the corpus (D-10 makes it a disposable projection; QUEUE 35 covers
# the exposure). .gitignore already excludes it, but that does not stop
# fossil: a `fossil addremove` in a checkout would commit it as a VERSIONED
# artifact -- permanent, synced to every peer, and removable only by
# shunning. This file is what stops that.
#
# Note the deliberate asymmetry: `viki cache push` puts the cache in the
# repo ON PURPOSE, as an unversioned (uv) file, which IS replaceable and is
# not history. Versioned is the accident; unversioned is the design.
.viki/*
